## Three tools, one question

.html ../slides-common/figures.html
.html figures/three-lenses.html

: The arc of the whole day. Three tools, three lenses on the same theme: what did the program actually do?
:
: 1. Race detector: ground truth about memory access ordering.
: 2. Execution tracer: ground truth about scheduling and time.
: 3. Delve: ground truth about program state, on demand.
:
: Keep this short — three sentences, not a lecture. The AI finale at the end of the day proves the point; don't oversell it here.

## What a data race actually is

Two goroutines accessing **the same memory location** at the same time,

where **at least one access is a write**,

with **no synchronization** ordering the accesses.

: Say the definition slowly. Every clause matters: two goroutines, same location, at least one write, no ordering.
:
: Everything else this hour follows from this definition.

## Why races are the worst kind of bug

- The classic "works on my machine" bug — the program may look correct for
  months, then corrupt data under production load.
- Nondeterministic by construction: whether it manifests depends on the
  schedule, the machine, the load.
- The detector turns that guesswork into a precise report with two stack
  traces.

: Races are the classic 'works on my machine' bug. The race detector turns guesswork into a precise report with two stack traces.
:
: Ask the room: who has shipped a race? Who found out from a customer?

## One more reason this matters in 2026

As AI agents write more of our code, engineers spend less time writing and more
time reviewing and debugging code they didn't write.

- A race report is **ground truth** — not an inference from reading source, by
  you *or* by an AI.
- Paste one into your AI assistant and it fixes the real bug. An agent with a
  race report fixes the real bug; an agent without one guesses.
- Mastering the tools that produce that evidence is the skill that compounds.

: Three sentences, not a lecture. This is the framing that bookends the day and gets cashed in by the two AI beats in the finale.

